  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CDW Government obligated $260M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. CDW Government won 655 awards so far, with an average award size of $396K, and obligations are down 5.4% year over year. Obligations trended from $451M in FY21 to $260M in FY26, showing smaller annual totals in the most recent years. The Department of Transportation is the largest buyer, accounting for $215M of obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computer Systems Design Services are the top markets, together accounting for more than half of current-year obligations through $129M and $99.9M respectively. Smaller buyers and markets include the Department of Defense at $14.6M, Department of Agriculture at $13.5M, and markets such as Other Computer Related Services at $19.1M and Software Publishers at $4.9M. This mix shows CDW Government concentrating on IT hardware and systems work for transportation and other civilian agencies while maintaining a broad buyer list across federal departments and international agencies.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are CDW Government's largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $215M to CDW Government, making it the largest customer in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $14.6M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $13.5M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $6.7M and the U.S. International Development Finance Corporation at $3.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and service markets drive CDW Government's obligations?",
        "body": "Electronic Computer Manufacturing is the largest market at $129M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $99.9M. Other Computer Related Services accounted for $19.1M and Software Publishers accounted for $4.9M. The portfolio includes hardware, systems design, and software categories across federal buyers."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does CDW Government make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "CDW Government obligated $260M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. CDW Government won 655 awards so far, with an average award size of $396K, and obligations are down 5.4% year over year. Historical obligations were $451M in FY21, $468M in FY22, $363M in FY23, $309M in FY24, and $274M in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from CDW Government?",
      "a": "The Department of Transportation is the largest buyer from CDW Government at $215M. Other federal buyers include the Department of Defense at $14.6M, Department of Agriculture at $13.5M, Department of Health and Human Services at $6.7M, and the U.S. International Development Finance Corporation at $3.4M. The buyer list also includes the Smithsonian Institution, Department of Justice, Department of Labor, Agency for International Development, and Department of State."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does CDW Government sell to the government?",
      "a": "CDW Government sells IT hardware, systems design, and software to the government. Electronic Computer Manufacturing accounted for $129M and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $99.9M in FY2026 to date. Other product and service markets include Other Computer Related Services at $19.1M and Software Publishers at $4.9M."
